-- a UUID sort key: Parquet orders UUID statistics bytewise while ClickHouse compares the two
-- 64-bit halves in the opposite order (issue #118371), so the bytewise min/max neither bound
-- the row group nor even stay in order. uuid2 holds the true top-1 behind its bytewise min
-- uuid3 is the same mismatch seen from the other side: its bytewise min is above its bytewise
-- max in ClickHouse order, which would be rejected as self-contradictory statistics
00000000-0000-0002-0000-000000000005
00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000a
00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000000a
